WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:04.879
When a Twitter user pointed out he could create
another social media platform for much less

00:00:04.879 --> 00:00:09.390
than his $44 billion dollar Twitter purchase
and reminded Musk that he apparently said

00:00:09.390 --> 00:00:14.560
he wouldn’t sell Tesla assets unless it
was to fund Mars, Musk responded: You might

00:00:14.560 --> 00:00:15.560
be right.

00:00:15.560 --> 00:00:20.490
If he walks away from the deal, he’s obligated
to pay a $1 billion termination fee.

00:00:20.490 --> 00:00:25.939
However, Musk reiterated he’s still committed
to buying Twitter in a follow-up tweet.

00:00:25.939 --> 00:00:29.779
Besides the fears and questions about how
the Twitter acquisition impacts Tesla and

00:00:29.779 --> 00:00:33.810
Tesla’s stock price, there’s been a whole
other tidal wave of criticism since the world

00:00:33.810 --> 00:00:36.010
found out that Elon Musk struck a deal to
buy Twitter.

00:00:36.010 --> 00:00:40.660
Here’s just some of the reaction from news
networks.

00:00:40.660 --> 00:00:45.220
You cannot let these guys control discourse
in this country or we are headed to hell.

00:00:45.220 --> 00:00:46.220
We are there.

00:00:46.220 --> 00:00:47.220
Trump opened the gates of hell and now they’re
chasing us down.

00:00:47.220 --> 00:00:50.810
If you get invited to something where there
are no rules, where there is total freedom,

00:00:50.810 --> 00:00:55.750
do you actually wanna go to that party, or
do you decide to stay home?

00:00:55.750 --> 00:00:58.860
And that’s a question for Twitter users.

00:00:58.860 --> 00:01:07.440
"If [the “neo-Nazi faction" of the GOP expands
in Nov.], we may look back on this .. as a

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:13.390
pivotal moment, when a petulant &amp; not-so-bright
billionaire casually bought one of the most

00:01:13.390 --> 00:01:17.610
influential messaging machines &amp; just handed
it to the far-right”

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:22.680
To that comment, Musk tweeted: “NBC basically
saying Republicans are Nazis”

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:27.510
Elon Musk’s $44 billion dollar purchase
of Twitter has clearly triggered an outpouring

00:01:27.510 --> 00:01:29.670
of disgust from some on the left.

00:01:29.670 --> 00:01:34.270
Twitter’s top lawyer, who earned $17 million
last year reportedly cried during a meeting

00:01:34.270 --> 00:01:35.840
about Musk’s takeover.

00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:39.530
Tennis star Martina Navratilova has vowed
she’ll never buy a Tesla.

00:01:39.530 --> 00:01:45.440
Democratic congresswoman Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez
is concerned about an explosion of hate crimes

00:01:45.440 --> 00:01:48.590
because a billionaire controls a massive communication
platform.

00:01:48.590 --> 00:01:52.630
To which Musk jokingly tweeted back: “Stop
hitting on me, I’m really shy”.

00:01:52.630 --> 00:01:58.310
AOC clarified she was referring to Mark Zuckerberg
before deleting her reply shortly after.

00:01:58.310 --> 00:02:01.840
Progressive users of Twitter who advocate
for progressive social justice causes have

00:02:01.840 --> 00:02:03.920
been nervous about the leadership change.

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:07.200
They fear Musk will promote conservative content
on Twitter.

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:09.530
And give those on the right a stronger voice.

00:02:09.530 --> 00:02:12.170
Musk has said he’ll allow Trump back on
the platform.

00:02:12.170 --> 00:02:15.569
During a recent Financial Times interview,
he called banning Trump a “morally bad decision…and

00:02:15.569 --> 00:02:16.569
foolish to the extreme.”

00:02:16.569 --> 00:02:17.569
“I think it was a morally bad decision,
to be clear.

00:02:17.569 --> 00:02:19.490
And foolish to the extreme,” he said

00:02:19.490 --> 00:02:23.120
He’s said timeouts are better than permanent
bans.

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:26.700
Conservatives have accused Twitter of censoring
them so they’re now cheering on Musk’s

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:32.230
takeover because he has vowed to reduce censorship
and bring more “free speech” to the platform.

00:02:32.230 --> 00:02:35.959
When Twitter prevented users from sharing
a New York Post article critical of Hunter

00:02:35.959 --> 00:02:40.920
Biden when his father was the then-Democratic
presidential nominee, Musk said it was “obviously

00:02:40.920 --> 00:02:42.760
incredibly inappropriate”.

00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:46.520
Twitter explained it banned the article because
of its policy on hacked materials.

00:02:46.520 --> 00:02:51.410
However, conservatives accuse the platform
of not applying that policy evenly.

00:02:51.410 --> 00:02:53.380
Musk is actually NOT a conservative.

00:02:53.380 --> 00:02:55.740
At best he might be described as a moderate.

00:02:55.740 --> 00:02:59.599
He said he was a registered independent when
he lived in California, the state he loudly

00:02:59.599 --> 00:03:01.380
left for Texas.

00:03:01.380 --> 00:03:05.630
He said he strongly supported Barack Obama
for president but believes “today’s Democratic

00:03:05.630 --> 00:03:08.580
Party has been hijacked by extremists.”

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:13.250
A meme he recently shared showed a person
who had leaned slightly left and was now surprised

00:03:13.250 --> 00:03:16.760
to find themselves right of center even though
their own views remained the same.

00:03:16.760 --> 00:03:21.629
That’s because according to the meme, the
“woke” left has drafted radically further

00:03:21.629 --> 00:03:22.880
to the left.

00:03:22.880 --> 00:03:26.689
Musk has made it known that he is out to save
the world and often touts his other ventures

00:03:26.689 --> 00:03:29.830
– Tesla and Space X - as being part of that
mission.

00:03:29.830 --> 00:03:34.300
In the same way, he believes free speech is
vital to saving democracy.

00:03:34.300 --> 00:03:38.160
Yet his critics believe too much free speech
is dangerous.

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:42.489
They wonder how Musk will deal with harassment
and disinformation on Twitter.

00:03:42.489 --> 00:03:46.920
Although Musk views Twitter as the digital
public town square, the left-leaning Guardian

00:03:46.920 --> 00:03:47.920
argues:

00:03:47.920 --> 00:03:51.910
“Twitter is less like a ‘town square’
and more like any Starbucks, McDonalds, or

00:03:51.910 --> 00:03:52.910
shopping center.

00:03:52.910 --> 00:03:59.069
It has other obligations and interests that
are at odds with completely unfettered speech.”

00:03:59.069 --> 00:04:02.230
Content moderation is difficult.

00:04:02.230 --> 00:04:06.409
The former Reddit CEO said Musk is “in for
a world of pain” and will “be forced to

00:04:06.409 --> 00:04:10.570
censor things” due to the difficulty of
enforcing free speech online.

00:04:10.570 --> 00:04:13.650
Musk didn’t appear to take his comments
seriously at the time.

00:04:13.650 --> 00:04:19.380
His response to the “novella of a thread”
as he called it was: “Twitter is way overdue

00:04:19.380 --> 00:04:21.470
for long form tweets!”

00:04:21.470 --> 00:04:25.130
Some observers compare the chatter from those
who have vowed to quit Twitter as akin to

00:04:25.130 --> 00:04:28.910
those who said they were moving to Canada
after Trump got elected.

00:04:28.910 --> 00:04:30.040
Most never followed through.

00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:33.940
If he decides to go ahead with his purchase
pending shareholder approval, Musk is counting

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:36.370
on his critics to stay on the platform.

00:04:36.370 --> 00:04:41.210
Tweeting: “I hope that even my worst critics
remain on Twitter, because that is what free

00:04:41.210 --> 00:04:43.370
speech means.”

00:04:43.370 --> 00:04:48.070
The news sent Twitter shares down more than
20% in premarket trading.

00:04:48.070 --> 00:04:51.090
Twitter’s stock price has been on a roller
coaster of a ride.

00:04:51.090 --> 00:04:53.720
There are so many other ways to grow your
